// Title: ScreenSaver Registry Key Set
// Sigma ID: 40b6e656-4e11-4c0c-8772-c1cc6dae34ce
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Jose Luis Sanchez Martinez (@Joseliyo_Jstnk)
// Date: 2022-05-04 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.011
// Description: Detects registry key established after masqueraded .scr file execution using Rundll32 through
//   desk.cpl
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of screen saver
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/VakninHai/status/1517027824984547329
//   - https://twitter.com/pabraeken/status/998627081360695297
//   - https://jstnk9.github.io/jstnk9/research/InstallScreenSaver-SCR-files
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_scr_file_executed_by_rundll32.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" and (RegistryKey contains "\\Control Panel\\Desktop\\SCRNSAVE.EXE" and RegistryValueData endswith ".scr") and (not((RegistryValueData contains "C:\\Windows\\System32\\" or RegistryValueData contains "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\")))
